cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the case-study data, please cite it as below."
title: "metric-discrimination-test: discriminability testing for self-reported metrics"
abstract: >-
  A dependency-free checker for the rule that a number is not a measurement
  until it has been observed to take different values on inputs that are known
  to differ. Includes five detectors for common failure signatures in
  self-reported metrics (constant, identity, bare zero, liveness bit, dead
  gate) and an anonymised case study of six instruments recorded in production
  on a continuously-running autonomous agent.
